WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.233 --> 00:00:01.534
This just in this morning.

00:00:01.534 --> 00:00:03.003
Time magazine has announced

00:00:03.003 --> 00:00:05.372
the 2022 person of the year

00:00:05.372 --> 00:00:06.840
who had the greatest influence

00:00:06.840 --> 00:00:08.975
on the events that you saw play out.

00:00:08.975 --> 00:00:09.442
Let's see what

00:00:09.442 --> 00:00:10.710
some of the finalists were.

00:00:10.710 --> 00:00:11.911
Elon Musk.

00:00:11.911 --> 00:00:13.813
Chinese President Xi Jinping.

00:00:13.813 --> 00:00:15.382
Protesters in Iran.

00:00:15.382 --> 00:00:17.183
Florida Governor Ron DeSantis.

00:00:17.183 --> 00:00:18.952
Congresswoman Liz Cheney.

00:00:18.952 --> 00:00:20.587
But the winner is Ukraine's

00:00:20.587 --> 00:00:21.855
President Zelensky,

00:00:21.855 --> 00:00:23.857
now battling his 10th month of war

00:00:23.857 --> 00:00:24.858
against the Russians

00:00:24.858 --> 00:00:27.160
ever since Putin invaded his country.

00:00:27.160 --> 00:00:29.062
And speaking of Ukraine's military,

00:00:29.062 --> 00:00:30.330
this morning, says that at least

00:00:30.330 --> 00:00:31.431
two people are dead.

00:00:31.431 --> 00:00:32.799
Several have been wounded

00:00:32.799 --> 00:00:33.533
after heavy

00:00:33.533 --> 00:00:34.901
Russian shelling targeted

00:00:34.901 --> 00:00:36.603
the civilian areas of the Donetsk

00:00:36.603 --> 00:00:38.038
and Harrison region.

00:00:38.038 --> 00:00:39.806
Meantime, in the midst of the fighting,

00:00:39.806 --> 00:00:40.874
there is some good news

00:00:40.874 --> 00:00:42.909
for families ahead of the holidays.

00:00:42.909 --> 00:00:44.177
Ukrainian soldiers

00:00:44.177 --> 00:00:45.211
returning home

00:00:45.211 --> 00:00:47.247
in a big prisoner exchange.

00:00:47.247 --> 00:00:48.214
CNN's Will Ripley

00:00:48.214 --> 00:00:50.517
has the exclusive reporting from Kiev.

00:00:53.820 --> 00:00:55.655
At an undisclosed location

00:00:55.655 --> 00:00:57.123
near the Russian border.

00:00:57.123 --> 00:00:57.957
Two busses

00:00:57.957 --> 00:01:00.326
arrive with 60 Ukrainian soldiers,

00:01:01.027 --> 00:01:02.462
prisoners of war

00:01:02.462 --> 00:01:04.531
just released in a P.O.W.

00:01:04.531 --> 00:01:06.332
swap with Russia.

00:01:06.332 --> 00:01:08.501
Two women. 58 men.

00:01:08.968 --> 00:01:11.538
Their first minutes of freedom,

00:01:11.538 --> 00:01:13.540
this marine tells me about his four year

00:01:13.540 --> 00:01:15.542
old daughter to my teenage daughter.

00:01:16.376 --> 00:01:18.445
It's so emotional, he says.

00:01:18.445 --> 00:01:18.812
I can't

00:01:18.812 --> 00:01:20.246
wait to tell her I love her

00:01:20.246 --> 00:01:22.615
and that I've missed her so much.

00:01:22.615 --> 00:01:25.652
Some are parents, others grandparents.

00:01:25.952 --> 00:01:28.221
Most defenders of Mariupol,

00:01:28.555 --> 00:01:30.390
the southern Ukrainian port city

00:01:30.390 --> 00:01:33.626
that fell to the Russians in May

00:01:33.626 --> 00:01:35.462
and some delivery by all of us

00:01:35.462 --> 00:01:37.664
from Mariupol worries so much, he says.

00:01:37.931 --> 00:01:39.265
We lost the city.

00:01:39.265 --> 00:01:41.034
We couldn't fight them off.

00:01:41.034 --> 00:01:41.401
We don't know

00:01:41.401 --> 00:01:44.270
how people will react to us.

00:01:44.270 --> 00:01:47.140
You'll get a hero's welcome, of course,

00:01:47.140 --> 00:01:48.374
as we go inside,

00:01:48.374 --> 00:01:50.376
they each get a cell phone

00:01:50.376 --> 00:01:51.811
the first time they've called

00:01:51.811 --> 00:01:54.080
their families in months.

00:01:54.080 --> 00:01:56.216
I cook. Mama. Papa. How's Mom?

00:01:56.282 --> 00:01:58.618
How's Dad? He asks. Are they alive?

00:02:00.520 --> 00:02:00.720
Their

00:02:00.720 --> 00:02:02.222
bodies bear the scars

00:02:02.222 --> 00:02:04.057
of months of captivity.

00:02:04.057 --> 00:02:05.325
Now, he didn't have any

00:02:05.325 --> 00:02:07.727
medical treatment, he says.

00:02:07.727 --> 00:02:09.295
It's been eight days

00:02:09.295 --> 00:02:11.598
since he's had a shower.

00:02:11.598 --> 00:02:12.899
A lot of these guys

00:02:12.899 --> 00:02:14.701
have physical injuries, scars.

00:02:14.701 --> 00:02:16.669
But the emotional scars,

00:02:16.669 --> 00:02:17.470
the mental scars

00:02:17.470 --> 00:02:18.705
from this kind of hellish ordeal

00:02:18.705 --> 00:02:20.473
are going to take even longer.

00:02:20.473 --> 00:02:21.407
To heal.

00:02:21.407 --> 00:02:23.309
One of the two rescue women,

00:02:23.309 --> 00:02:25.411
a radio intelligence operator,

00:02:25.411 --> 00:02:28.548
describes months of psychological torture

00:02:29.015 --> 00:02:32.051
lies that half of Ukraine was now part

00:02:32.051 --> 00:02:35.155
of Russia brainwashing, forced to read

00:02:35.155 --> 00:02:38.324
Russian poetry, sing Russian songs,

00:02:38.625 --> 00:02:40.994
pledge loyalty, to mother Russia

00:02:41.761 --> 00:02:42.629
as a kid.

00:02:42.795 --> 00:02:44.998
I wondered, when will this be over?

00:02:45.031 --> 00:02:47.800
She says. And now you're here.

00:02:47.800 --> 00:02:49.969
Sorry for my tears giving you so much

00:02:50.670 --> 00:02:52.438
for this former P.O.W.

00:02:52.438 --> 00:02:54.407
There are no tears left.

00:02:54.407 --> 00:02:55.141
Her six year

00:02:55.141 --> 00:02:56.609
old daughter is still in

00:02:56.609 --> 00:02:58.311
occupied Mariupol.

00:02:58.311 --> 00:03:00.513
She has no way to contact her

00:03:00.513 --> 00:03:02.916
or her husband, a sailor.

00:03:02.916 --> 00:03:04.984
They surrender on the same day.

00:03:05.518 --> 00:03:06.686
How does it feel to be out

00:03:06.686 --> 00:03:07.720
and know that your husband

00:03:07.720 --> 00:03:09.956
still still there, still in Russia,

00:03:09.956 --> 00:03:11.090
which can see no reason

00:03:11.090 --> 00:03:13.393
why I worry so much about him, she says.

00:03:13.960 --> 00:03:16.229
They torture men much more than women.

00:03:16.563 --> 00:03:17.897
She's not ready to talk about

00:03:17.897 --> 00:03:20.166
how she was physically treated.

00:03:20.166 --> 00:03:21.534
She, like everyone

00:03:21.534 --> 00:03:22.902
here, just wants to see

00:03:22.902 --> 00:03:25.371
family wants to go home.

00:03:25.371 --> 00:03:26.806
For most from devastated

00:03:26.806 --> 00:03:28.741
and occupied Mariupol

00:03:28.741 --> 00:03:30.677
going home is not an option

00:03:31.711 --> 00:03:32.345
for

00:03:34.113 --> 00:03:35.348
one of the first things they did

00:03:35.348 --> 00:03:36.849
was seeing the Ukrainian anthem

00:03:36.849 --> 00:03:38.484
that you heard the beginning of there.

00:03:38.484 --> 00:03:39.886
Because in Russia every day

00:03:39.886 --> 00:03:41.621
they were forced to wake up at 6 a.m.

00:03:41.621 --> 00:03:43.223
to the Russian anthem

00:03:43.223 --> 00:03:44.557
and they said all they wanted to do

00:03:44.557 --> 00:03:45.858
is be back on their home soil.

00:03:45.858 --> 00:03:48.027
They are now back on their home soil.

00:03:48.027 --> 00:03:49.329
But it is a long road ahead.

00:03:49.329 --> 00:03:50.630
They don't get to go directly home.

00:03:50.630 --> 00:03:51.898
One because many of their homes

00:03:51.898 --> 00:03:52.999
have been destroyed.

00:03:52.999 --> 00:03:53.766
In Mariupol,

00:03:53.766 --> 00:03:54.801
but also they need to go through

00:03:54.801 --> 00:03:56.035
a rehabilitation program

00:03:56.035 --> 00:03:58.204
to try to transition back to normal life.

00:03:58.204 --> 00:03:59.372
And after everything,

00:03:59.372 --> 00:04:01.074
all the horrific things they experienced

00:04:01.074 --> 00:04:02.141
and they've been through.

00:04:02.242 --> 00:04:04.777
It'll only be a very tough recovery for

00:04:04.777 --> 00:04:05.912
these men and women.

00:04:07.113 --> 00:04:07.981
Yeah, it's hard to see

00:04:07.981 --> 00:04:10.083
what a normal life is like for them.

00:04:10.083 --> 00:04:10.917
Will Ripley.

00:04:10.917 --> 00:04:11.851
Thank you, Don.

00:04:11.851 --> 00:04:13.086
Poppy, just hearing the stories

00:04:13.086 --> 00:04:13.820
of those people

00:04:13.820 --> 00:04:14.287
who are

00:04:14.287 --> 00:04:16.022
released from being prisoners of war,

00:04:16.022 --> 00:04:16.756
but now

00:04:16.756 --> 00:04:17.490
they're still separated

00:04:17.490 --> 00:04:18.191
from their families.

00:04:18.191 --> 00:04:18.992
They're still trying to figure out

00:04:18.992 --> 00:04:20.493
what life looks like now.

00:04:20.493 --> 00:04:22.629
And you're so right, there is no normalcy

00:04:23.029 --> 00:04:23.696
after that.

